================================================================================
                      1. INTRODUCTION
================================================================================

1.1 PURPOSE
-----------

The SOAR (Security Orchestration, Automation and Response) Unified API provides
a centralized backend for security operations. It integrates with Wazuh and
OpenSearch to fetch alerts, enrich them with external threat intelligence,
calculate risk scores, recommend patches, filter noise, and automate response
playbooks.

1.2 ARCHITECTURE OVERVIEW
-------------------------

The API is organized into six functional teams:

  TEAM 0: Core Data
  - Fetches alerts from Wazuh/OpenSearch
  - Provides unified data normalization
  - Optional parallel enrichment with VT, AbuseIPDB, MISP

  TEAM 1: Risk Scoring
  - Calculates risk scores (0-100) based on multiple factors
  - Determines priority levels (LOW/MEDIUM/HIGH/CRITICAL)
  - Provides confidence metrics

  TEAM 2: Patch Recommendation
  - Analyzes alerts for vulnerable software
  - Queries NVD (National Vulnerability Database) for CVE details
  - Queries EPSS (Exploit Prediction Scoring System) for exploit likelihood
  - Provides prioritized patch recommendations

  TEAM 3: Log Filtering & Noise Reduction
  - LLM-assisted alert classification
  - Distinguishes between noise and important alerts
  - Uses rule ID, severity, statistics, and context features

  TEAM 4: Playbooks
  - Tag-based decision logic
  - Risk-score threshold evaluation
  - Automated action recommendations (QUARANTINE, BLOCK, INVESTIGATE, etc.)

  TEAM 5: Threat Intel
  - IOC lookup in VirusTotal, AbuseIPDB, MISP
  - CVE extraction from alert descriptions
  - EPSS and CVSS score retrieval
  - MISP event synchronization

1.3 TECHNOLOGY STACK
--------------------

  - Framework: FastAPI (Python)
  - Web Server: Uvicorn
  - Database: OpenSearch
  - Intelligence Sources: VirusTotal, AbuseIPDB, MISP, NVD, EPSS
  - HTTP Client: httpx (async)

================================================================================
                      2. QUICK START
================================================================================

2.1 PREREQUISIRES
-----------------

  - Python 3.9+
  - OpenSearch instance (for alert storage)
  - MISP instance (for threat intelligence)
  - VirusTotal API key
  - AbuseIPDB API key (optional)

2.2 ENVIRONMENT CONFIGURATION
------------------------------

Set the following environment variables before starting the API:

  +-------------------+---------------------------------------------------+
  | Variable          | Description                                       |
  +-------------------+---------------------------------------------------+
  | OS_HOST           | OpenSearch host URL (e.g., http://localhost:9200)|
  | OS_PORT           | OpenSearch port (default: 9200)                  |
  | OS_USER           | OpenSearch username                              |
  | OS_PASS           | OpenSearch password                              |
  | VT_API_KEY        | VirusTotal API key                               |
  | MISP_URL          | MISP instance URL                                |
  | MISP_KEY          | MISP API key                                     |
  | ABUSEIPDB_KEY     | AbuseIPDB API key (optional)                     |
  +-------------------+---------------------------------------------------+

Example (.env file):

  OS_HOST=http://localhost:9200
  OS_PORT=9200
  OS_USER=admin
  OS_PASS=admin
  VT_API_KEY=your_virustotal_api_key
  MISP_URL=https://misp.example.com
  MISP_KEY=your_misp_api_key

2.3 RUNNING THE API
-------------------

  # Install dependencies
  pip install -r requirements.txt

  # Run the server
  uvicorn main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000

  # Or using the module directly
  python -m uvicorn main:app --reload

The API will be available at: http://localhost:8000

Auto-generated API documentation (Swagger UI):
  http://localhost:8000/docs

================================================================================
                 3. API ENDPOINTS - DETAILED REFERENCE
================================================================================

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3.1 ALERTS - TEAM 0: CORE DATA
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ENDPOINT: GET /api/v1/alerts/

DESCRIPTION:
  Fetches Wazuh alerts from OpenSearch with optional parallel enrichment.
  When enrich=true, each alert is enriched concurrently against VirusTotal,
  AbuseIPDB, and MISP using asyncio.gather with return_exceptions=True.

QUERY PARAMETERS:

  +-----------------+--------+---------+--------------------------------------+
  | Parameter       | Type   | Default | Description                          |
  +-----------------+--------+---------+--------------------------------------+
  | limit           | int    | 100     | Number of alerts to fetch (1-1000)  |
  | offset (alias: from) | int | 0       | Number of alerts to skip            |
  | severity        | int    | None    | Filter by Wazuh rule level (1-15)    |
  | enrich          | bool   | false   | Enable external intelligence        |
  +-----------------+--------+---------+--------------------------------------+

EXAMPLE REQUEST:

  curl -X GET "http://localhost:8000/api/v1/alerts/?limit=10&enrich=true"

EXAMPLE RESPONSE:

  [
    {
      "event_id": "wazuh-alerts-2024.01.15-001",
      "source": "wazuh",
      "timestamp": "2024-01-15T10:30:00Z",
      "description": "sshd: authentication failed for root from 192.168.1.50",
      "severity": 5,
      "host_context": {
        "hostname": "prod-web-01",
        "ip_address": "192.168.1.100",
        "mac_address": "00:11:22:33:44:55",
        "os_name": "Ubuntu 22.04 LTS"
      },
      "enrichment_data": {
        "vt_score": 45,
        "abuse_score": 72,
        "epss_score": 0.85,
        "cvss_score": 7.8,
        "risk_score": 68,
        "misp_matches": [],
        "tags": ["suspicious", "ssh", "brute-force"],
        "debug_info": {}
      },
      "raw_data": {
        "rule": {"id": 5710, "level": 5},
        "full_log": "Jan 15 10:30:00 prod-web-01 sshd[12345]: Failed password for root from 192.168.1.50 port 22 ssh2",
        "srcip": "192.168.1.50"
      }
    }
  ]

BEHAVIOR DETAILS:

  - Parallel Enrichment: When enrich=true, all alerts are processed in parallel
    using asyncio.gather. Each alert's enrichment (VT, AbuseIPDB, MISP) also
    runs in parallel within each alert.

  - Timeouts: Individual enrichment service calls are capped at 5 seconds.

  - Fail-Soft: Uses return_exceptions=True so one failing enrichment never
    kills the rest of the batch.

  - Safe Defaults: For internal/private IP addresses:
    - vt_score = 0 (clean)
    - abuse_score = 100 (safe)
    - enrichment is skipped

  - Batch Protection: Entire enrichment process continues even if some
    alerts fail, returning safe defaults for failed ones.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3.2 RISK SCORE - TEAM 1: RISK SCORING
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ENDPOINT: POST /api/v1/risk-score/

DESCRIPTION:
  Calculates a comprehensive risk score (0-100) for an alert based on:
  - Base severity from Wazuh rule level
  - VirusTotal reputation score
  - AbuseIPDB confidence score
  - CVSS (Common Vulnerability Scoring System) score
  - EPSS (Exploit Prediction Scoring System) score

REQUEST BODY:

  {
    "alert": UnifiedAlert
  }

EXAMPLE REQUEST:

  curl -X POST "http://localhost:8000/api/v1/risk-score/" \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d '{
      "alert": {
        "event_id": "alert-001",
        "source": "wazuh",
        "timestamp": "2024-01-15T10:30:00Z",
        "description": "Web shell detected",
        "severity": 12,
        "host_context": {
          "hostname": "prod-app-01",
          "ip_address": "10.0.0.50"
        },
        "raw_data": {},
        "enrichment_data": {
          "vt_score": 95,
          "abuse_score": 85,
          "cvss_score": 9.8,
          "epss_score": 0.97
        }
      }
    }'

EXAMPLE RESPONSE:

  {
    "event_id": "alert-001",
    "risk_score": 94,
    "priority": "CRITICAL",
    "confidence": 0.85,
    "features": {
      "base_severity": 120,
      "enrichment": 149.85,
      "cvss": 9.8,
      "epss": 0.97
    }
  }

RISK SCORING ALGORITHM:

  1. Base Score = severity * 10
     - Severity range: 1-15
     - Base score range: 10-150

  2. Enrichment Score Components:
     - CVSS contribution: cvss * 5 (max: 49)
     - EPSS contribution: epss * 50 (max: 50)
     - Abuse score contribution: abuse_score * 0.5 (max: 50)
     - VT score contribution: vt_score * 0.5 (max: 50)

  3. Final Score = min(base_score + enrichment_score, 100)

  4. Priority Mapping:
     - Score > 70: CRITICAL
     - Score > 30: HIGH
     - Score <= 30: MEDIUM
     - (Note: Score 0-30 returns LOW in current implementation)

  5. Confidence: Fixed at 0.85 (85%)

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3.3 PATCH RECOMMENDATION - TEAM 2: PATCH RECOMMENDATION
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ENDPOINT: POST /api/v1/patch/

DESCRIPTION:
  Analyzes alerts to identify vulnerabilities and retrieves patch
  recommendations from NVD (National Vulnerability Database) and
  EPSS (Exploit Prediction Scoring System).

REQUEST BODY:

  {
    "alert": UnifiedAlert
  }

EXAMPLE REQUEST:

  curl -X POST "http://localhost:8000/api/v1/patch/" \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d '{
      "event_id": "vuln-alert-001",
      "source": "wazuh",
      "timestamp": "2024-01-15T10:30:00Z",
      "description": "Vulnerable OpenSSL version detected - CVE-2023-1234",
      "severity": 10,
      "host_context": {
        "hostname": "prod-db-01",
        "ip_address": "192.168.2.10"
      },
      "raw_data": {},
      "enrichment_data": {
        "tags": ["vuln:CVE-2023-1234"]
      }
    }'

EXAMPLE RESPONSE:

  {
    "host": "prod-db-01",
    "recommendations": [
      {
        "cve": "CVE-2023-1234",
        "cvss": 9.8,
        "epss": 0.95,
        "priority": "CRITICAL",
        "action": "Apply OpenSSL 3.0.8 or later immediately"
      },
      {
        "cve": "CVE-2023-5678",
        "cvss": 7.5,
        "epss": 0.72,
        "priority": "HIGH",
        "action": "Schedule security update within 7 days"
      }
    ]
  }

RESPONSE DETAILS:

  - host: Hostname of the affected system

  - recommendations: Array of patch recommendations sorted by priority
    - cve: CVE identifier (e.g., CVE-2023-1234)
    - cvss: CVSS v3.1 base score (0-10)
    - epss: EPSS probability (0-1, representing exploit likelihood)
    - priority: CRITICAL/HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW based on CVSS and EPSS
    - action: Human-readable recommended action

CVSS SCORING INTERPRETATION:
  - 9.0-10.0: CRITICAL
  - 7.0-8.9: HIGH
  - 4.0-6.9: MEDIUM
  - 0.1-3.9: LOW

EPSS SCORING INTERPRETATION:
  - >= 0.9: Very likely to be exploited
  - 0.5-0.89: Likely to be exploited
  - 0.1-0.49: Possible exploitation
  - < 0.1: Unlikely exploitation

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3.4 FILTERING - TEAM 3: LOG FILTERING & NOISE REDUCTION
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ENDPOINT: POST /api/v1/alerts/filter

DESCRIPTION:
  LLM-assisted classification to distinguish between noise alerts and
  important security events. Uses multiple features including rule ID,
  severity, event frequency, IP reputation, and asset criticality.

REQUEST BODY:

  {
    "alerts": [UnifiedAlert, ...]
  }

EXAMPLE REQUEST:

  curl -X POST "http://localhost:8000/api/v1/alerts/filter" \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d '{
      "alerts": [
        {
          "event_id": "noise-alert-001",
          "source": "wazuh",
          "timestamp": "2024-01-15T10:30:00Z",
          "description": "IDS alert",
          "severity": 3,
          "host_context": {
            "hostname": "dev-server",
            "ip_address": "192.168.10.50"
          },
          "raw_data": {
            "rule": {"id": 100001},
            "stats": {"event_count_5m": 150, "unique_ips": 50},
            "context": {"asset_criticality": "low"}
          },
          "enrichment_data": {
            "vt_score": 5
          }
        },
        {
          "event_id": "important-alert-001",
          "source": "wazuh",
          "timestamp": "2024-01-15T10:35:00Z",
          "description": "Multiple SSH authentication failures",
          "severity": 8,
          "host_context": {
            "hostname": "prod-app-01",
            "ip_address": "192.168.1.100"
          },
          "raw_data": {
            "rule": {"id": 5710},
            "stats": {"event_count_5m": 5, "unique_ips": 1},
            "context": {"asset_criticality": "high"}
          },
          "enrichment_data": {
            "vt_score": 75
          }
        }
      ]
    }'

EXAMPLE RESPONSE:

  [
    {
      "alert_id": "noise-alert-001",
      "classification": "noise",
      "confidence": 0.88,
      "summary": "Rule 100001 marked as noise"
    },
    {
      "alert_id": "important-alert-001",
      "classification": "important",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "summary": "Rule 5710 marked as important"
    }
  ]

FEATURES USED FOR CLASSIFICATION:

  1. rule_id: Wazuh rule identifier (known noisy vs. important rules)
  2. severity: Alert severity level (1-15)
  3. description: Alert description text
  4. event_count_5m: Number of events in last 5 minutes (high = likely noise)
  5. unique_ips: Number of unique source IPs (high = likely noise/spam)
  6. ip_reputation: VirusTotal score (high = suspicious)
  7. asset_criticality: Criticality of the affected asset (high/medium/low)

CLASSIFICATION LOGIC:
  - High event_count_5m (>50): Likely noise from repeated scanning
  - High unique_ips (>10): Likely mass scanning/spamming
  - High IP reputation (>50): Indicates malicious activity
  - High asset_criticality + low noise indicators: Important
  - Low severity + high noise indicators: Noise

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3.5 PLAYBOOKS - TEAM 4: PLAYBOOKS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ENDPOINT: POST /api/v1/playbooks/decision

DESCRIPTION:
  Unified decision engine combining tag-based logic with risk-score
  thresholds to recommend automated or manual actions.

REQUEST BODY:

  {
    "alert": UnifiedAlert
  }

EXAMPLE REQUESTS:

  # Example 1: High-risk malware alert
  curl -X POST "http://localhost:8000/api/v1/playbooks/decision" \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d '{
      "alert": {
        "event_id": "malware-001",
        "source": "wazuh",
        "timestamp": "2024-01-15T10:30:00Z",
        "description": "Trojan detected",
        "severity": 15,
        "host_context": {
          "hostname": "workstation-john",
          "ip_address": "192.168.5.100"
        },
        "raw_data": {},
        "enrichment_data": {
          "vt_score": 100,
          "risk_score": 98
        }
      }
    }'

  # Response
  {
    "action": "QUARANTINE_HOST",
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "automation_level": "AUTO",
    "reason": "Critical severity with very high risk score (98) - immediate quarantine recommended"
  }

  # Example 2: Low-risk informational alert
  curl -X POST "http://localhost:8000/api/v1/playbooks/decision" \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d '{
      "alert": {
        "event_id": "info-001",
        "source": "wazuh",
        "timestamp": "2024-01-15T10:30:00Z",
        "description": "User logged in",
        "severity": 3,
        "host_context": {
          "hostname": "dev-server",
          "ip_address": "192.168.10.20"
        },
        "raw_data": {},
        "enrichment_data": {
          "vt_score": 0,
          "risk_score": 15
        }
      }
    }'

  # Response
  {
    "action": "LOG_AND_MONITOR",
    "confidence": 0.90,
    "automation_level": "MANUAL",
    "reason": "Low severity and low risk score - informational only, no action required"
  }

AVAILABLE ACTIONS:

  +---------------------------+-------------------------------------------+
  | Action                   | Description                               |
  +---------------------------+-------------------------------------------+
  | QUARANTINE_HOST          | Isolate affected host from network       |
  | BLOCK_IP                 | Block malicious IP at firewall/IDS       |
  | ISOLATE_SERVICE         | Isolate compromised service/container    |
  | INVESTIGATE              | Initiate deeper forensic investigation    |
  | CREATE_TICKET            | Create alert ticket for analyst review    |
  | SEND_SOC_ALERT           | Alert SOC team via email/Slack/PagerDuty |
  | RUN_PLAYBOOK            | Execute automated response playbook       |
  | LOG_AND_MONITOR         | Log only, continue monitoring            |
  | NO_ACTION               | No action required                        |
  +---------------------------+-------------------------------------------+

AUTOMATION LEVELS:

  - AUTO: Fully automated action
  - SEMI: Automatic with human approval required
  - MANUAL: Analyst review required

DECISION LOGIC:

  1. If risk_score >= 80:
     - AUTOMATION_LEVEL: AUTO
     - Action: QUARANTINE_HOST (if critical severity)

  2. If risk_score >= 60:
     - AUTOMATION_LEVEL: SEMI
     - Action: BLOCK_IP or INVESTIGATE

  3. If tags contain "malware" or "ransomware":
     - AUTOMATION_LEVEL: AUTO
     - Action: QUARANTINE_HOST

  4. If tags contain "phishing":
     - AUTOMATION_LEVEL: SEMI
     - Action: CREATE_TICKET

  5. If severity <= 3 and risk_score <= 20:
     - AUTOMATION_LEVEL: MANUAL
     - Action: LOG_AND_MONITOR

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3.6 THREAT INTEL - TEAM 5: THREAT INTEL
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ENDPOINT A: POST /api/v1/threat-intel/lookup

DESCRIPTION:
  Looks up IP addresses or other IOCs in external threat intelligence
  sources (VirusTotal, AbuseIPDB, MISP) and returns aggregated results.

REQUEST BODY:

  {
    "alert": UnifiedAlert
  }

EXAMPLE REQUEST:

  curl -X POST "http://localhost:8000/api/v1/threat-intel/lookup" \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d '{
      "event_id": "intel-lookup-001",
      "source": "wazuh",
      "timestamp": "2024-01-15T10:30:00Z",
      "description": "Suspicious outbound connection",
      "severity": 8,
      "host_context": {
        "hostname": "prod-server",
        "ip_address": "185.220.101.1"
      },
      "raw_data": {},
      "enrichment_data": {}
    }'

EXAMPLE RESPONSE:

  {
    "ioc": "185.220.101.1",
    "malicious": true,
    "reputation": 12,
    "sources": ["VirusTotal", "AbuseIPDB", "MISP"]
  }

RESPONSE DETAILS:

  - ioc: The indicator of compromise that was looked up
  - malicious: Boolean indicating if any source flagged as malicious
  - reputation: Composite score (0-100, lower = more malicious)
  - sources: List of sources that provided positive matches

VIRUSTOTAL SCORE CALCULATION:
  - percentage = (malicious detections / total detections) * 100
  - Example: 65 malicious, 20 suspicious, 15 harmless = 65/100 * 100 = 65%

ABUSEIPDB SCORE:
  - Direct confidence score from AbuseIPDB (0-100)
  - Score > 25 typically indicates malicious activity

MISP MATCHES:
  - Any match in MISP automatically sets malicious=true, reputation=0

PRIVATE IP HANDLING:
  - Private IP ranges (10.x.x.x, 192.168.x.x, 172.16-31.x.x) are not
    looked up in external sources
  - Returns: malicious=false, reputation=100, sources=[]
  - CVEs are still extracted and scored for private IPs

------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ENDPOINT B: POST /api/v1/threat-intel/misp-sync

DESCRIPTION:
  Synchronizes recent OpenSearch alerts with MISP to find existing
  threat intelligence matches. Fetches last 50 alerts and queries MISP
  for each unique IP address.

REQUEST BODY:
  None required (empty POST)

EXAMPLE REQUEST:

  curl -X POST "http://localhost:8000/api/v1/threat-intel/misp-sync"

EXAMPLE RESPONSE:

  {
    "status": "success",
    "synced_events": 3,
    "events": [
      {
        "event_id": "wazuh-alerts-2024.01.15-001",
        "ip": "192.168.1.50",
        "misp_matches": 5
      },
      {
        "event_id": "wazuh-alerts-2024.01.15-002",
        "ip": "10.0.0.25",
        "misp_matches": 2
      },
      {
        "event_id": "wazuh-alerts-2024.01.15-003",
        "ip": "185.220.101.45",
        "misp_matches": 12
      }
    ]
  }

RESPONSE DETAILS:

  - status: "success" or "error"
  - synced_events: Number of events with at least one MISP match
  - events: Array of events with MISP matches
    - event_id: OpenSearch event identifier
    - ip: Source IP that was queried
    - mips_matches: Number of MISP events matching this IP

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3.7 HEALTH CHECK
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ENDPOINT: GET /health

DESCRIPTION:
  Checks connectivity to core services (OpenSearch and MISP).
  Returns 200 OK if healthy, 503 Service Unavailable if a critical
  service is unreachable.

EXAMPLE SUCCESS RESPONSE:

  {
    "status": "healthy",
    "opensearch": "connected",
    "misp": "connected"
  }

EXAMPLE FAILURE RESPONSE:

  HTTP/1.1 503 Service Unavailable

  {
    "detail": "OpenSearch (core database) is unreachable"
  }

HEALTH CHECK LOGIC:

  1. OpenSearch Check:
     - GET /_cluster/health on OpenSearch
     - Returns "connected" if HTTP 200
     - If fails: returns 503 error

  2. MISP Check:
     - GET /users/view/me on MISP
     - Returns "connected" if HTTP 200
     - If fails: "disconnected" (non-critical, warning only)

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3.8 ROOT ENDPOINT
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ENDPOINT: GET /

DESCRIPTION:
  Simple endpoint to verify the API is running.

EXAMPLE RESPONSE:

  {
    "status": "SOAR API is online",
    "version": "v1"
  }

================================================================================
                    4. DATA MODELS - COMPLETE REFERENCE
================================================================================

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4.1 CORE SCHEMAS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

HOSTCONTEXT
  +---------------+-------------+----------------------------------------+
  | Field         | Type        | Description                            |
  +---------------+-------------+----------------------------------------+
  | hostname      | string      | Hostname of the alert source           |
  | ip_address    | string      | Primary IP address (IPv4/IPv6)        |
  | mac_address   | string|null | MAC address (optional)                 |
  | os_name       | string|null | Operating system name (optional)       |
  +---------------+-------------+----------------------------------------+

ENRICHMENTDATA
  +---------------+-----------------+--------------------------------------+
  | Field         | Type            | Description                          |
  +---------------+-----------------+--------------------------------------+
  | vt_score      | int             | VirusTotal detection percentage      |
  |               |                 | (0-100, 0 = clean/not scored)        |
  | abuse_score   | int             | AbuseIPDB confidence score (0-100)   |
  |               |                 | (0 = clean/not scored)               |
  | epss_score    | float|null      | EPSS probability (0-1)               |
  | cvss_score    | float|null      | CVSS base score (0-10)               |
  | risk_score    | int|null        | Risk score (0-100)                   |
  | misp_matches  | list[string]    | MISP event UUIDs                     |
  | tags          | list[string]    | Enrichment tags (e.g., "misp_hit")   |
  | debug_info    | dict            | Per-service error messages           |
  +---------------+-----------------+--------------------------------------+

UNIFIEDALERT
  +-------------------+-------------+-------------------------------------+
  | Field             | Type        | Description                         |
  +-------------------+-------------+-------------------------------------+
  | event_id          | string      | Unique alert identifier            |
  | source            | string      | Alert source (e.g., "wazuh")        |
  | timestamp         | datetime    | Alert timestamp (ISO 8601)         |
  | description       | string      | Human-readable alert description    |
  | severity          | int         | Wazuh rule level (1-15)            |
  | host_context      | HostContext | Host information                   |
  | raw_data          | dict        | Original raw alert data            |
  | enrichment_data   | EnrichmentData | Enriched data (defaults provided)|
  +-------------------+-------------+-------------------------------------+

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4.2 TEAM-SPECIFIC SCHEMAS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

RISKSCOREREQUEST
  {
    "alert": UnifiedAlert
  }

RISKSCORERESPONSE
  +---------------+--------+------------------------------------------------+
  | Field         | Type   | Description                                    |
  +---------------+--------+------------------------------------------------+
  | event_id      | string | Alert's unique identifier                     |
  | risk_score    | int    | Calculated risk score (0-100)                  |
  | priority      | string | Priority (LOW/MEDIUM/HIGH/CRITICAL)            |
  | confidence    | float  | Confidence score (0-1)                          |
  | features      | dict   | Score breakdown                                |
  +---------------+--------+------------------------------------------------+

PATCHRESPONSE
  +------------------+--------+-------------------------------------------+
  | Field            | Type   | Description                               |
  +------------------+--------+-------------------------------------------+
  | host             | string | Affected hostname                         |
  | recommendations | list   | Array of Recommendation objects           |
  +------------------+--------+-------------------------------------------+

RECOMMENDATION
  +----------+--------+---------------------------------------------------+
  | Field    | Type   | Description                                       |
  +----------+--------+---------------------------------------------------+
  | cve      | string | CVE identifier                                    |
  | cvss     | float  | CVSS score                                        |
  | epss     | float  | EPSS probability                                  |
  | priority | string | Priority level                                   |
  | action   | string | Recommended action                               |
  +----------+--------+---------------------------------------------------+

FILTERREQUEST
  {
    "alerts": List[UnifiedAlert]
  }

FILTERRESULT
  +------------------+--------+-------------------------------------------+
  | Field            | Type   | Description                               |
  +------------------+--------+-------------------------------------------+
  | alert_id         | string | Unique alert identifier                  |
  | classification   | string | "noise" or "important"                    |
  | confidence       | float  | Classification confidence (0-1)          |
  | summary          | string | Human-readable summary                    |
  +------------------+--------+-------------------------------------------+

PLAYBOOKDECISIONREQUEST
  {
    "alert": UnifiedAlert
  }

PLAYBOOKDECISIONRESPONSE
  +------------------+--------+-------------------------------------------+
  | Field            | Type   | Description                               |
  +------------------+--------+-------------------------------------------+
  | action           | string | Recommended action                        |
  | confidence       | float  | Decision confidence (0-1)                |
  | automation_level | string | AUTO/SEMI/MANUAL                         |
  | reason           | string | Human-readable explanation                |
  +------------------+--------+-------------------------------------------+

INTELRESPONSE
  +-------------+--------+--------------------------------------------------+
  | Field       | Type   | Description                                      |
  +-------------+--------+--------------------------------------------------+
  | ioc         | string | Indicator of Compromise                         |
  | malicious   | bool   | Whether flagged as malicious                    |
  | reputation | int    | Reputation score (0-100, lower = worse)         |
  | sources     | list   | Sources providing positive matches              |
  +-------------+--------+--------------------------------------------------+

MISPSYNCRESPONSE
  +------------------+--------+-------------------------------------------+
  | Field            | Type   | Description                               |
  +------------------+--------+-------------------------------------------+
  | status          | string | "success" or "error"                      |
  | synced_events    | int    | Number of events synced                   |
  | events          | list   | Array of synced events                    |
  +------------------+--------+-------------------------------------------+

================================================================================
                    5. INTEGRATION DETAILS
================================================================================

5.1 EXTERNAL INTEGRATIONS
--------------------------

VIRUSTOTAL
  - Endpoint: https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/
  - Rate Limit: 4 requests/minute (public API)
  - Data: IP reputation, malware detections, related domains
  - API Key: Required in VT_API_KEY environment variable

ABUSEIPDB
  - Endpoint: https://api.abuseipdb.com/api/v2/
  - Rate Limit: Varies by subscription tier
  - Data: IP reputation, abuse reports, country blocking
  - API Key: Required in ABUSEIPDB_KEY environment variable

MISP (Malware Information Sharing Platform)
  - Endpoint: Configured MISP instance URL
  - Features: IOC sharing, threat actor tracking, galaxy clusters
  - Authentication: API key in header

NVD (National Vulnerability Database)
  - Endpoint: https://services.nvd.nist.gov/rest/json/cves/2.0
  - Data: CVE details, CVSS scores, affected software
  - Rate Limit: 6 requests per second (6 calls in 10 sec window)

EPSS (Exploit Prediction Scoring System)
  - Endpoint: https://api.first.org/data/v1/epss
  - Data: Probability of exploitation in next 30 days
  - Update: Daily data feed

OPENSEARCH
  - Default Index: wazuh-alerts-*
  - Authentication: Basic auth (OS_USER, OS_PASS)
  - Connection: HTTP (non-SSL by default)

5.2 PARALLEL PROCESSING
-----------------------

The API implements parallel processing at multiple levels:

  Level 1: Batch Alert Processing
  - Uses asyncio.gather() to process multiple alerts concurrently
  - return_exceptions=True prevents one failure from stopping the batch

  Level 2: Per-Alert Enrichment
  - VT, AbuseIPDB, and MISP lookups run in parallel
  - Each service has 5-second timeout

  Level 3: CVE Score Fetching
  - NVD and EPSS lookups run in parallel for all CVEs found

5.3 FAIL-SOFT ARCHITECTURE
---------------------------

The system is designed with fail-soft principles:

  1. Service Timeouts: 5 second max per external service call
  2. Exception Handling: return_exceptions=True in gather calls
  3. Safe Defaults:
     - Internal IPs: vt_score=0, abuse_score=100
     - Failed lookups: keep existing values or use defaults
  4. Debug Info: All errors captured in enrichment_data.debug_info

================================================================================
                    6. ADVANCED FEATURES
================================================================================

6.1 ENRICHMENT PIPELINE
-----------------------

The enrichment pipeline executes in this order:

  1. IP Enrichment (parallel)
     - VirusTotal IP lookup
     - AbuseIPDB IP lookup
     - MISP IP search

  2. CVE Extraction
     - Regex scan of description and raw_data
     - Pattern: CVE-YYYY-NNNN (or CVE-YYYY-NNNNN+)
     - Tag format: vuln:CVE-YYYY-NNNN

  3. CVE Scoring (if CVEs found, parallel)
     - EPSS score lookup
     - NVD CVSS score lookup
     - Store maximum values across all CVEs

  4. Tag Population
     - "misp_hit" if MISP match found
     - "vuln:CVE-*" for each CVE found

6.2 CVE EXTRACTION
------------------

The CVE extraction engine:

  1. Searches alert.description and alert.raw_data for CVE pattern
  2. Extracts unique CVEs found
  3. Adds "vuln:CVE-YYYY-NNNN" tags
  4. Queries NVD and EPSS for each CVE
  5. Stores maximum CVSS and EPSS across all CVEs

Example:
  Alert: "Buffer overflow in Apache 2.4.49 - CVE-2021-41773 and CVE-2021-42013"
  -> Tags: ["vuln:CVE-2021-41773", "vuln:CVE-2021-42013"]
  -> epss_score: 0.98 (max)
  -> cvss_score: 9.8 (max)

6.3 RISK SCORING ALGORITHM
--------------------------

Detailed algorithm breakdown:

  BASE_SCORE = severity * 10
  // severity 1-15 -> base_score 10-150

  ENRICHMENT_SCORE =
    + (cvss_score or 0) * 5       // max ~50
    + (epss_score or 0) * 50      // max ~50
    + (abuse_score or 0) * 0.5    // max ~50
    + (vt_score or 0) * 0.5       // max ~50

  FINAL_SCORE = min(BASE_SCORE + ENRICHMENT_SCORE, 100)

  PRIORITY =
    if FINAL_SCORE > 70: "CRITICAL"
    else if FINAL_SCORE > 30: "HIGH"
    else: "MEDIUM" (actually returns LOW in code)

6.4 PLAYBOOK DECISION LOGIC
----------------------------

The playbook decision engine uses a multi-factor evaluation:

  Input Factors:
  - alert.severity (1-15)
  - alert.enrichment_data.risk_score (0-100)
  - alert.enrichment_data.tags
  - alert.enrichment_data.vt_score
  - alert.enrichment_data.abuse_score
  - alert.description (keyword detection)

  Decision Matrix:
  +-------------------+-------------------+-------------------+
  | Condition         | Automation        | Action            |
  +-------------------+-------------------+-------------------+
  | Risk >= 90        | AUTO              | QUARANTINE_HOST   |
  | Risk 70-89        | SEMI              | BLOCK_IP          |
  | Risk 50-69        | SEMI              | INVESTIGATE       |
  | Risk < 50         | MANUAL            | LOG_AND_MONITOR   |
  | Tag contains      | AUTO              | QUARANTINE_HOST   |
  | "malware"         |                   |                   |
  | Tag contains      | SEMI              | CREATE_TICKET     |
  | "phishing"        |                   |                   |
  | Severity >= 12    | SEMI              | SEND_SOC_ALERT    |
  +-------------------+-------------------+-------------------+

================================================================================
                    7. ERROR HANDLING
================================================================================

7.1 HTTP STATUS CODES
---------------------

  +-------+---------------------------------------------------------------+
  | Code  | Meaning                                                        |
  +-------+---------------------------------------------------------------+
  | 200   | Success - Request completed normally                         |
  | 400   | Bad Request - Invalid query parameters or malformed JSON     |
  | 422   | Unprocessable Entity - Validation error (Pydantic)          |
  | 500   | Internal Server Error - Unexpected server error             |
  | 503   | Service Unavailable - External dependency unreachable       |
  +-------+---------------------------------------------------------------+

7.2 ERROR RESPONSE FORMAT
-------------------------

  {
    "detail": "Error description here"
  }

Example - OpenSearch unreachable:
  HTTP 503
  {
    "detail": "OpenSearch (core database) is unreachable"
  }

Example - Validation error:
  HTTP 422
  {
    "detail": [
      {
        "loc": ["body", "alert", "severity"],
        "msg": "ensure this value is less than or equal to 15",
        "type": "value_error"
      }
    ]
  }

7.3 SERVICE AVAILABILITY
-------------------------

Critical Services (required):
  - OpenSearch: API returns 503 if unavailable at startup or health check

Non-Critical Services (optional):
  - MISP: Shown as "disconnected" in health check, but API remains functional
  - VirusTotal: Fail-soft, returns vt_score=0 on failure
  - AbuseIPDB: Fail-soft, returns abuse_score=0 on failure
  - NVD: Fail-soft, cvss_score remains None on failure
  - EPSS: Fail-soft, epss_score remains None on failure

================================================================================
                    8. TROUBLESHOOTING
================================================================================

8.1 COMMON ISSUES
----------------

  Issue: "Missing mandatory environment variable: OS_HOST"
  Solution: Ensure OS_HOST is set in environment variables

  Issue: "OpenSearch (core database) is unreachable" (503)
  Solution:
    - Verify OpenSearch is running
    - Check OS_HOST, OS_PORT, OS_USER, OS_PASS settings
    - Verify network connectivity to OpenSearch

  Issue: Enrichment returns vt_score=0, abuse_score=100
  Cause: Likely a private/internal IP (skipped external lookups)
  Solution: This is expected behavior for non-routable IPs

  Issue: "VT exception: 403 Forbidden"
  Solution: Verify VT_API_KEY is valid and has API access

  Issue: "MISP connection refused"
  Solution:
    - Verify MISP_URL is correct
    - Verify MISP_KEY is valid
    - Check network connectivity to MISP instance

  Issue: Slow response times with enrich=true
  Cause: Parallel enrichment processes up to 100 alerts simultaneously
  Solution:
    - Reduce limit parameter
    - External services may be slow (5s timeout each)

8.2 DEBUG INFORMATION
---------------------

Enrichment errors are stored in alert.enrichment_data.debug_info:

  {
    "enrichment_data": {
      "debug_info": {
        "vt_error": "VT exception: ...",
        "abuse_error": "AbuseIPDB exception: ...",
        "misp_error": "MISP exception: ...",
        "epss_error_cve-2024-1234": "...",
        "nvd_parse_error_cve-2024-5678": "..."
      }
    }
  }

Logs are available with prefix markers:
  - [Alerts]: Alert fetching and processing
  - [Intel]: Threat intelligence enrichment
  - [CVE]: CVE extraction and scoring
  - [Monitor]: Incoming/outgoing service calls

================================================================================
                    9. RATE LIMITS & BEST PRACTICES
================================================================================

RATE LIMITS BY SERVICE:

  +---------------+---------------+----------------------------------+
  | Service       | Rate Limit    | Notes                            |
  +---------------+---------------+----------------------------------+
  | VirusTotal    | 4/minute      | Public API, consider caching    |
  | AbuseIPDB     | Variable      | Depends on subscription tier     |
  | NVD           | 6/second      | NIST official limits             |
  | EPSS          | None          | Free API, updated daily          |
  | MISP          | Variable      | Depends on instance configuration|
  +---------------+---------------+----------------------------------+

BEST PRACTICES:

  1. Pagination: Use offset parameter for large result sets
  2. Enrichment: Use sparingly - each alert makes up to 3 external calls
  3. Caching: Consider implementing caching for repeat lookups
  4. Timeouts: Default 5s per service call - adjust if needed
  5. Monitoring: Check /health endpoint for service status

